'''All Gamers|AG电子竞技俱乐部''', often abbreviated as '''AG''', is a [[:Category:China|Chinese]] esports organization.

{{GameArticle}}
==History==
'''All Gamers|AG电子竞技俱乐部''' is the first professional e-sports team in China, founded by Hu Haibin(胡海滨), Zhang Lei(张磊Jeeps), Chen Yu/Han Yu Liang(陈宇/寒羽良), Yi Ran(易冉YR), Wei QiDi ([[starcraft:Deep|韦奇迪Deep]]) and Ma Tianyuan([[starcraft:MTY|马天元 MTY]]) on October 1, 1999.

Originally, '''AG''' was a ''[[starcraft:StarCraft|StarCraft:Brood War]]'' clan, officially known as "'''=A.G=|AsiaGame'''", and it won the first world championship in Chinese e-sports history in the 2v2 StarCraft event at the World Cyber Games 2001 ([[starcraft:World_Cyber_Games/2001|WCG 2001]]).

In 2008, Jiang Yafei(姜亚斐/菲菲) established the team '''F.C_World''' for [[CrossFire]] in Chengdu (referred to as '''FC''').In 2009, Ma Tianyuan([[starcraft:MTY|马天元 MTY]]) and Sun Liewei([[warcraft:xiaOt|孙力伟 xiaOt]]) formed the '''V.A e-sports club|VA电子竞技俱乐部''' in Wuhan. In 2010, Jiang Yafei(姜亚斐/菲菲)  led the '''FC team''' to join the '''V.A e-sports club''' and renamed it as '''All Gamers|AG电子竞技俱乐部'''. Jiang Yafei(姜亚斐/菲菲) , Ma Tianyuan([[starcraft:MTY|马天元 MTY]])  and Yi Ran(易冉YR) became the founders of the team.

In 2015, with Ma Tianyuan([[starcraft:MTY|马天元 MTY]])  and Yi Ran(易冉YR) withdrawing due to family reasons, Jiang Yafei(姜亚斐/菲菲) took over as the CEO of '''AG''' .In 2019, Le Kedeng(乐可登) joined '''AG''' , and together they led the team to continue its development.Now the '''AG''' team is a Chinese professional esports organization with teams in [[CrossFire]], [[Counter-Strike_(series)|Counter-Strike]], [[League of Legends]], [[PUBG_Mobile|PUBG Mobile]], [[Honor_of_Kings|Honor of Kings]], [[VALORANT]] and others.

In order to better participate in international events such as [[Esports World Cup]], the '''AG''' has carried out internationalization and established '''AG.AL International'''. On August 23, 2026, at the [[Esports_World_Cup/2026|EWC 2026]], the '''AG.AL International''' surpassed its opponents with a total score of 5300 points and won the club championship, achieving the best result for Chinese e-sports clubs in history, beating [[Team Falcons]] and [[Team Vitality]] on second to last day of the championship. Le Kedeng(乐可登) represents '''AG'''  raising the EWC Club Championship Trophy in Paris.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://esportsworldcup.com/en/press-releases/agal-crowned-ewc26-club-champion|title=AG.AL Crowned Esports World Cup 2026 Club Champion After Landmark Competition in Paris|publisher='''[[Esports World Cup]]'''|date=2026-08-24}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.globaltimes.cn/page/202608/1368903.shtml|title=Chinese club AG.AL wins 2026 Esports World Cup as Macron hands over the trophy, 25 years after China’s first esports gold|author=Jiang Li|publisher=Global Times|date=2026-08-24}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=https://pokde.net/gaming/esports/ag-al-wins-ewc26|title=AG.AL Wins Esports World Cup 2026 Club Championship In Paris|author=Low Boon Shen|publisher=Pokde.Net|date=2028-08-27}}</ref>

