'''Alliance''' is a professional esports organization originally founded under GoodGame in April 2013.<ref name="Alliance founded">{{cite web|url=https://www.gosugamers.net/news/23584-alliance-picks-up-nth-and-naniwa|title=Alliance picks up NTH and Naniwa|date=2013-04-12|publisher=[[GosuGamers]]|language={{FlagNoLink|usuk}} English}}</ref> In 2016 it was announced that Alliance would become an independant, player-owned organization as they departed from its parent company GoodGame.<ref name="Alliance EG player owned">{{cite web|url=https://www.espn.com/esports/story/_/id/18262358/2016-evil-geniuses-alliance-leave-parent-company-goodgame|title=Evil Geniuses and Alliance become player-owned organizations|date=2016-12-12|author=[[Jacob Wolf]]|publisher=[[ESPN]]|language={{FlagNoLink|usuk}} English}}</ref>

{{GameArticle}}

==Corporate History==
In April 2013, '''Alliance''' was founded, picking up the Dota 2 team [[:dota2:No Tidehunter|No Tidehunter]] and StarCraft 2 player [[:starcraft2:Naniwa|Naniwa]].<ref name="Alliance founded"/>

When [[Riot Games]] introduced a new 'sale of sponsorship' rule on November 21st, 2014. Good Game Agency and Alex Garfield who owned the '''Alliance''' and [[Evil Geniuses]] brands, pulled the brands from ''League of Legends''.<ref name="sale of sponsorship">{{cite web|url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160815122939/http://www.dailydot.com/esports/riot-games-ownership-rule/|title=Riot Games introduces new 'sale of sponsorships' rule|date=2014-11-22|author=[[Samuel Lingle]]|publisher=[[The Daily Dot]]|language={{FlagNoLink|usuk}} English}}</ref> '''Alliance''' would later then rebrand into [[Elements]].<ref name="Elements">{{cite web|url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160305015115/http://www.dailydot.com/esports/alliance-rebrands-elements/|title=By their powers combined, Alliance is now Elements|date=2015-01-08|author=[[Samuel Lingle]]|publisher=[[The Daily Dot]]|language={{FlagNoLink|usuk}} English}}</ref>

On December 12, 2016, the organization announced that it would become an independent organization after parting with their parent organization ''GoodGame''.<ref name="Alliance independant">{{cite web|url=https://medium.com/@alliancegg/alliance-shifts-into-independent-organisation-806733fbb5ce#.5kr4rjyb4|title=Alliance shifts into independent organisation|date=2016-12-12|author='''Alliance'''|publisher=[[Medium]]|language={{FlagNoLink|usuk}} English}}</ref>

