'''Dplus''' (previously known as '''DWG KIA''' and '''Damwon Gaming''') is a [[:Category:South Korea|Korean]] esports organization. They are currently competing under the official name of '''Dplus KIA''' due to sponsorship with [[wikipedia:Kia|KIA]].

{{GameArticle}}

==History==
===Corporate History===
Damwon Gaming, founded and partially owned by Kim "[[leagueoflegends:Micro|Micro]]" Mok-kyoung, originally started as '''MiraGe Gaming''' in 2017. Damwon Gaming got its name after receiving a full sponsorship from Damwon on May 28th, 2017<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://www.facebook.com/dpluskia.lol/posts/pfbid02DG7K3hsmZ5Hp6vKjSK6MsXC9FHDYrEs5Wyi9MXuVowBq5Cg5cGu9KWK2po6rMpMQl|title=DAMWON Gaming(DWG) 으로 팀명을 바꿔서 활동합니다!|trans_title=We will start competing under the name Damwon Gaming(DWG)!|author=Dplus KIA|date=2017-05-28|language={{FlagNoLink|kr}} Korean}}</ref>. [[leagueoflegends:Micro|Micro]] sold his share of the organization as he resigned as head coach in February 2020<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://www.facebook.com/ppitagi/posts/2617174351738558|title=안녕하세요. 담원게이밍 감독 김목경 입니다.|trans_title=Hello. This is Kim Mok-kyoung, head coach of Damwon Gaming.|author=[[leagueoflegends:Micro|Micro]]|date=2020-02-24|language={{FlagNoLink|kr}} Korean}}</ref>.

Damwon Gaming started competing under the name '''DWG KIA''' due to sponsorship with [[wikipedia:Kia|KIA]] in January 2021<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://m.sports.naver.com/esports/article/005/0001398649|title=담원 기아, 새 유니폼·엠블럼 공개|trans_title=DWG KIA Reveals New Uniform and Emblem|author=이다니엘|date=2021-01-07|language={{FlagNoLink|kr}} Korean|publisher=KUKMINILBO}}</ref>. The organization rebranded to '''Dplus''' in January 2023 and have since competed under the name of '''Dplus KIA'''.<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://m.sports.naver.com/esports/article/468/0000913245|title=담원 기아→디플러스 기아로 새 출발 "글로벌 구단 도약 초석 다질 것"|trans_title=DWG KIA Takes a Fresh Start with the New Name Dplus KIA "Will set firm foundations towards being a global organization"|author=김민규|date=2023-01-09|language={{FlagNoLink|kr}} Korean|publisher=스포츠서울}}</ref>

