'''FaZe Clan''' was founded as a YouTube channel on May 30th, 2010, by players Eric "CLipZ" Rivera, Jeff "House Cat" Emann (later renamed to "Timid") and Ben "Resistance" Christensen under the name '''FaZe Sniping'''. <ref>{{cite web|url=https://twitter.com/FaZeClan/status/497191279504011264|title=Correct answer was Resistance, Housecat, and Clipz!|date=|date_est=2014-08-06|author='''FaZe Clan'''}}</ref> The clan originally uploaded ''Call of Duty'' montages, before expanding into real-life content years later.

At the end of 2011, '''FaZe Clan''' stepped into competitive play with a ''[[callofduty:Modern Warfare 3|Call of Duty: Modern Warfare 3]]'' lineup.

In November 2014, '''FaZe Clan''' announced the creation of [[Red Reserve]], a subsidiary organization. <ref>{{cite web|url=https://youtu.be/8ustZoDImLM|title=FaZe: #RED - A Multi-CoD Teamtage by FaZe Barker|date=|date_est=2014-11-01|author='''FaZe Clan'''}}</ref> In 2016, [[Red Reserve]] cut ties with '''FaZe''' to operate under their own banner.

