'''Gentle Mates''' is a [[:Category:France|French]] esports organization.

{{GameArticle}}

==History==
Gentle Mates was originally founded by Squeezie, Gotaga and Brawks on April 13th, 2023<ref name="Gentle Mates formed">{{cite web|url=https://twitter.com/gentlemates/status/1646562429042556964|title=Tout commence ici ...|trans_title=It all starts here...|language={{Flag|fr}} French|date=2023-04-13|author='''Gentle Mates'''}}</ref>, after already existing under the name "SBG" since January 2nd, 2023 in [[valorant:VCL/2023/France/Split_1|VCL France 2023 Split 1]]. The team announced a [[fortnite:Gentle_Mates|Fortnite]] division the following day. After having already won Split 1 of VCL Challengers France 2023, Gentle  Mates won [[valorant:VCL/2023/France/Split_2|Split 2]] and qualified to [[valorant:VCL/2023/Ascension/EMEA|Ascension EMEA 2023]] which they won in a 3-0 victory over [[Apeks]]<ref name="Ascension 2023">{{cite web|url=https://twitter.com/valleague_emea/status/1680642963142062080|title=YOUR VCT ASCENSION EMEA 2023 CHAMPIONS: GENTLE MATES|date=2023-07-16|author=[[VALORANT Challengers EMEA]]}}</ref>, qualifying to the 2024 and 2025 VCT EMEA Leagues, marking their first time joining a Tier 1 esports environment. 

Before the start of the 2024 esports season, Gentle Mates joined Teamfight Tactics, League of Legends and Rocket League. They also joined Age of Empires on March 22nd, 2024, which is to date their most succesful game, with their sole player [[ageofempires:MarineLorD|MarineLorD]] winning 3/3 S-Tier events in that year. After signing a Call of Duty roster exclusively for [[Esports World Cup/2024]], the team officially aquired the [[callofduty:Call of Duty League|Call of Duty League]] slot of the Los Angeles Guerillas, rebrading the team to [[callofduty:Los_Angeles_Guerrillas_M8|Los Angeles Guerrillas M8]]<ref name="m8">{{cite web|url=https://x.com/gentlemates/status/1864419554010792026|title=Dream Comes True, Gentle Mates Arrives in COD League|date=2024-12-04|author=[[Gentle Mates]]}}</ref> 
