'''Guild Esports''' was a [[:Category:United Kingdom|British]] esports organization founded in June 2020. It is co-owned by former football star [[wikipedia:David Beckham|David Beckham]]. On the 18th of January 2022, '''Guild Esports''' sign a sponsorship with the crypto exchange company [https://www.bitstamp.net Bitstamp] in a deal worth $6.1 million.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://dotesports.com/business/news/guild-esports-signs-sponsorship-crypto-exchange-bitstamp|title=Guild Esports signs $6.1 million sponsorship with crypto exchange Bitstamp|author=[https://dotesports.com/author/mateuszmiter Mateusz Miter]|publisher=[https://dotesports.com Dot Esports]|date=2022-01-18}}</ref>

{{GameArticle}}

==Competitive History==
On June 25, 2020, '''Guild Esports''' officially launched.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://twitter.com/guildesports/status/1275927157206913030|title=#WeAreGuild|date=2020-06-25|author='''Guild Esports'''}}</ref> Shortly after on July 23, they announced their first team by acquiring former ''Rocket League'' roster of ''[[:rocketleague:Team Singularity|Team Singularity]]'', consisting of ''[[:rocketleague:Tho|Tho]]'', ''[[:rocketleague:ScrubKilla|ScrubKilla]]'', and ''[[:rocketleague:noly|noly]]''.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.guildesports.com/rocketleague|title=GUILD ESPORTS LAUNCHES INTO ROCKET LEAGUE|date=2020-07-23|author='''Guild Esports'''}}</ref> On October 23, '''Guild Esports''' acquired ''[[:valorant:Bonk|Bonk]]'', a [[:Category:Sweden|Swedish]] ''VALORANT'' team.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://twitter.com/guildesports/status/1318870173210771456|title=THE HUNT BEGINS|date=2020-10-21|author='''Guild Esports'''}}</ref> Only 3 weeks later, ''FIFA'' player ''[[:easportsfc:NRaseck|NRaseck]]'' was signed, who formely played for [[:easportsfc:Rogue|Rogue]].<ref>{{cite web|url=https://twitter.com/guildesports/status/1291282851984486401|title=Guild is proud to enter @EAFIFAesports with @NRaseck7. Welcome to the team, champ|date=2020-08-06|author='''Guild Esports'''}}</ref>

At the end of 2020 and the beginning of 2021, '''Guild Esports''' signed 4 ''Fortnite'' players including ''[[:fortnite:Hen|Hen]]'', who later took home the first big tournament win for '''Guild''' by winning ''[[:fortnite:Fortnite_Champion_Series/Chapter_2/Season_5/Grand_Finals/Europe|C2S5: FNCS - Grand Finals: Europe]]'' in March 2021. In April, the ''Rocket League'' team managed to win their first big tournament: ''[[:rocketleague:Rocket_League_Championship_Series/Season_X/Spring/Europe/3|RLCS Season X - Spring: EU Regional Event 3]]'' by surprisingly defeating ''[[:rocketleague:Team BDS|Team BDS]]'', who had won nearly every event they played that season, twice.

