==Corporate History==
LOUD was founded on February 28, 2019, by Bruno "PlayHard" Oliveira, Jean Ortega, and Mathew Ho as a Brazilian esports organization.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://ge.globo.com/esports/noticia/2023/12/11/vinicius-junior-se-torna-socio-da-loud.ghtml|title=Vinícius Júnior se torna sócio da LOUD|date=2023-12-11|author=ge.globo}}</ref> Initially focused on Free Fire, LOUD quickly gained traction by combining competitive gaming with content creation, becoming a dominant force in digital entertainment.

In its early days, LOUD built a strong community through YouTube and social media, pioneering a content-driven approach that helped esports players and influencers gain mainstream recognition. By May 2020, the organization became the first esports brand in the world to surpass 1 billion views on YouTube.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.theenemy.com.br/free-fire/loud-alcanca-a-marca-de-1-bilhao-de-views-no-youtube|title=LOUD alcança a marca de 1 bilhão de views no YouTube|date=2020-05-18|author=The Enemy}}</ref>

Expanding beyond Free Fire, LOUD entered Fortnite, League of Legends (LoL), and Valorant. In 2020, LOUD joined the CBLOL (Campeonato Brasileiro de League of Legends) franchise system, establishing itself in Brazil’s premier LoL competition.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://ge.globo.com/esports/lol/noticia/2022/08/31/final-do-cblol-2022-historia-loud-explodiu-no-conteudo-antes-de-sucesso-esportivo.ghtml|title=Final do CBLOL 2022: História da LOUD explodiu no conteúdo antes de sucesso esportivo|date=2022-08-31|author=ge.globo}}</ref> The team won CBLOL 2022 Split 2, securing a spot at the Worlds 2022.

LOUD also became a powerhouse in Valorant, winning the VCT 2022 Champions and finishing runner-up at VCT 2023 LOCK//IN São Paulo.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://liquipedia.net/valorant/LOUD|title=LOUD - Liquipedia VALORANT Wiki|date=2023|author=Liquipedia}}</ref> Their international success solidified LOUD as a top-tier esports organization.

Beyond competition, LOUD cultivated one of the largest esports communities in Latin America, amassing over 50 million followers across platforms. In December 2023, professional footballer Vinícius Júnior joined LOUD as a partner and ambassador, broadening the brand’s reach and involvement in social initiatives.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://forbes.com.br/forbes-games/2023/12/vini-jr-vira-socio-da-loud-em-movimentacao-inedita-para-os-e-sports-brasileiros/|title=Vini Jr. vira sócio da LOUD em movimentação inédita para os e-sports brasileiros|date=2023-12-11|author=Forbes Brasil}}</ref>

LOUD continues to grow, expanding into new gaming ecosystems and business ventures. The organization remains at the forefront of esports and content creation, securing its place as a global leader in the gaming industry.

