'''OpTic Gaming''' is a professional esports organization formed by [[KR3W]] in 2006. Their current owner and CEO is [[H3CZ]]. It was also owned by ''Infinite Esports & Entertainment'' and ''Immortals Gaming Club'' from 2016 to November 2020.

{{GameArticle}}

==Competitive History==
{{todo|Add more competitive history}}
In 2006, '''OpTic Gaming''' was founded as a Call of Duty sniping clan. Their first venture into esports was in 2010, with the signing of their [[:callofduty:OpTic Gaming|Call of Duty team]], featuring the likes of [[:callofduty:NaDeSHoT|NaDeSHoT]], [[:callofduty:Vengeance|Vengeance]], [[:callofduty:Merk|Merk]] and [[:callofduty:FLawLesS|FLawLesS]]. They have since then shaped themselves into the most known Call of Duty team within their community, and have branched out to various other esports. 

In 2019, [[:callofduty:OpTic Gaming Los Angeles|OpTic Gaming Los Angeles]] was announced as a franchise member of the newly formed ''Call of Duty League'', this spot was sold to [[100 Thieves]] and renamed to [[:callofduty:Los Angeles Thieves|Los Angeles Thieves]], as '''OpTic''' was reacquired by [[H3CZ]], which would result in the organization rebranding the existing [[:callofduty:Chicago Huntsmen|Chicago Huntsmen]] team into [[:callofduty:OpTic Chicago|OpTic Chicago]].

