==Corporate History==
In 2016, ''Infinite Esports & Entertainment'' became the company behind the '''OpTic Gaming''' brand, which would see [[H3CZ]] lose a lot of control of the organization. They were bought out in 2019 by ''Immortals Gaming Club'', which resulted in [[H3CZ]] stepping down from his role and the '''OpTic''' brand.<ref name="H3CZ steps down">{{cite web|url=https://www.igc.gg/press-61219|title=Immortals Gaming Club acquires Infinite Esports & Entertainment, parent of OpTic Gaming|date=2019-09-15|author=[[Immortals Gaming Club]]|publisher=[[Immortals Gaming Club]]|language={{Flag|usuk}} English}}</ref> On november 11th, 2020, [[H3CZ]] reacquired '''OpTic Gaming''' from ''Immortals Gaming Club'', with all of the teams playing under the brand staying under the ownership of ''IGC''.<ref name="H3CZ returns">{{cite web|url=https://twitter.com/optic/status/1326570392006307850|title=Hector Rodriguez reacquires OpTic Gaming brand from Immortals Gaming Club|date=2020-11-11|author='''OpTic Gaming'''|publisher=Twitter|language={{Flag|usuk}} English}}</ref> [[OpTicJ]], one of the founders of '''OpTic''', left the organization following the reacquisition.

On the 4th of April in 2015, [[:callofduty:Nadeshot|Nadeshot]] retired from competitive Call of Duty, this would result in him becoming a co-CEO of the '''OpTic Gaming''' team,<ref name="Nadeshot CEO">{{cite web|url=https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=FjOBGFMPmJs|title=I Have Something to Tell You Guys..|date=2015-04-04|author=[[:callofduty:Nadeshot|Nadeshot]]|publisher=Youtube|language={{Flag|usuk}} English}}</ref> he left the organization with the creation of [[100 Thieves]], his own organisation and clothing brand.<ref name="Nadeshot leaves">{{cite web|url=https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=R3gQ65NP0Ck|title=STARTING MY OWN TEAM?|date=2016-03-06|author=[[:callofduty:NaDeSHoT|NaDeSHoT]]|publisher=Youtube|language={{Flag|usuk}} English}}</ref>

In January 2018, '''OpTic Gaming''' signed [[:dota2:Maelk|Maelk]] as their Chief Gaming Officer,<ref name="Maelk joins">{{cite web|url=https://www.hltv.org/news/22402/north-announce-whimp-as-new-director-of-esports|date=2018-01-27|title=North announce new Director of Esports|author=[[LucasAM]]|publisher=[[HLTV]]}}</ref> as the organization had grown into five different games at that point. He left the organization to join [[100 Thieves]] in June 2019.<ref name="Maelk leaves">{{cite web|url=https://twitter.com/100Thieves/status/1141459738539913216|title=Excited to welcome Jacob Toft-Andersen (@TheMaelk) to 100 Thieves as our new VP of Esports!|date=2019-06-19|author=[[100 Thieves]]|publisher=Twitter|language={{Flag|usuk}} English}}</ref>

