==Controversy==
===IEM XII Katowice PUBG Invitational===
In February 2018, [[ESL]] held the 12th Season of the Intel Extreme Masters, hosting the [[:pubg:Intel Extreme Masters/Season XII/Katowice|IEM XII Katowice PUBG Invitational]] event. '''OpTic Gaming''' attended and managed to win 2 of the 8 rounds in the event, but they were disqualified from the final round after their player [[:pubg:Bahawaka|Bahawaka]] used a wall glitch to get an unfair advantage over opposing teams. This resulted in them moving from second to fifth place, losing out on $12,000 in prizemoney.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.pcgamer.com/optic-gaming-loses-dollar12000-pubg-prize-after-being-disqualified-for-cheating/|title=OpTic Gaming loses $12,000 PUBG prize after being disqualified for cheating|date=2018-03-09|author=''PCGamer.com''|publisher=''PCGamer.com''|language={{Flag|usuk}} English}}</ref>

===eXTREMESLAND ZOWIE Asia 2018===
In 2018, '''OpTic Gaming'''  tried supporting the Indian esports scene by fielding their [[:counterstrike:OpTic India|OpTic India]] team, which took the Asian Counter-Strike scene by storm. During the [[:counterstrike:EXTREMESLAND_ZOWIE_Asia_CS:GO_2018|eXTREMESLAND 2018 Finals]], [[:counterstrike:forsaken|forsaken]] was caught using cheats.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.hltv.org/news/25118/forsaken-caught-cheating-at-extremesland-optic-india-disqualified|title=forsaken caught cheating at eXTREMESLAND; OpTic India disqualified|date=2018-10-19|author=[[Professeur]]|publisher=[[HLTV]]}}</ref>

This resulted in the immediate disbandment of the team with the statement: "We stand strongly against any form of cheating as it not only tarnishes the local roster, but potentially harms competitive integrity of the region. We have terminated Nikhil '[[:counterstrike:forsaken|forsaken]]' Kumawat's contract for his actions. At this time we are also releasing the remaining roster to pursue new opportunities with other competitive options".<ref>{{cite web|url=https://twitter.com/OpTicIndia/status/1053342722122268672|title=OpTic India release team|date=2018-10-19|author=[[OpTic India]]}}</ref>

