'''Team Falcons''' (known as '''Falcons Esports''' prior to late 2022) is a [[:Category:Saudi Arabia|Saudi Arabian]] esports organization.

{{GameArticle}}

==History==
'''Team Falcons''' was founded on December 28th, 2017 when they first announced their ''FIFA'' team roster.<ref name="Falcons">{{Cite web |url=https://x.com/TeamFalconsGG/status/946468053700636673|title=We are proud to announce the first Saudi FIFA E-Sports team, Team Falcons. We are also proud to introduce our team members |date=2017-12-28|author='''Team Falcons'''}}</ref> With Mossad "[[easportsfc:Msdossary|Msdossary]]" Aldossary being one of the co-founders, and also serving as the team's CEO, he also represented the organization in FIFA. As a player, he left the organization between 2018 to 2021 where he competed for organizations such as [[Rogue]] and [[Tundra Esports]], in which he returned to represent the organization as a player.<ref name="Msdossary FIFA return>{{Cite web |url=https://x.com/TeamFalconsGG/status/1447577470828531714|title=THE KING IS BACK.|date=2021-10-11|author='''Team Falcons'''}}</ref> 

In August 2022, Grant Rousseau joined Team Falcons as their Global Director of Esports.<ref name="Grant Rousseau joins>{{Cite web |url=https://esportsinsider.com/2022/08/grant-rousseau-joins-team-falcons|title=Grant Rousseau joins Team Falcons|date=2022-08-11|author=Ivan Šimić|publisher=Esports Insider}}</ref> He would later leaves the organization on late August 2025 to join [[Ninjas in Pyjamas]].<ref name="Grant Rousseau leaves">{{cite web|url=https://x.com/GrantRous/status/1959697652867801260|title=The end of an era|author=Grant Rousseau|date=2025-08-24}}</ref> Jordan "[[counterstrike:Next|Next]]" Savelli replace his position on the organization by December 2025.<ref name="Next joins">{{cite web|url=https://x.com/_next/status/1998718560223506642|title=Excited to step in as Global Director of Esports at Team Falcons!|author=Next|date=2025-12-10}}</ref>

